# 217: wrong arity, too MANY arguments — and the singular. A 1-parameter
# function says "1 argument", not "1 arguments". §4 makes the wording a
# contract, which is exactly why the plural lives in one `error.rs` helper
# instead of at two call sites that would each guess.
--- source
fn one(a) { return a; }
print one(1, 2);
--- expect
error: Type at line 2: one expects 1 argument, got 2
